## arg 1:  the new package version
## arg 2:  the old package version, if applicable

post_install() {
  cat << 'EOM'

╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║  Study Notes — offline, local-first study notes                  ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Your notes live entirely on this machine — no cloud, no telemetry.

  Data directory : ~/.local/share/study-notes/
    Database     : ~/.local/share/study-notes/study-notes.db
    Image assets : ~/.local/share/study-notes/assets/

On first launch the app seeds a "Getting Started" section with a
welcome note covering the 4-level hierarchy, keyboard shortcuts,
and backup tips.

Backups (plain compressed tarballs, easy to schedule with cron):

  Create : tar -czf study-notes-backup-$(date +%F_%H%M%S).tar.gz \
               -C ~/.local/share study-notes
  Restore: tar -xzf <backup>.tar.gz -C ~/.local/share

Or use the bundled scripts from the source repository:
  scripts/backup-data.sh / scripts/restore-data.sh

The app makes zero outbound network connections (enforced by CSP).

EOM
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
